  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 3,
  "questionLabels": [],
  "question": {
    "text": "For a reaction taking place in three steps at same temperature, overall rate constant <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfrac></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ea</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>Ea</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Ea</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>40</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>50</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo> </mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> respectively, the overall <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ea</mi></math> is _________ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math>.",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "30",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>According to Arrhenius concept,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Ae</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Given that,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>.</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math></p><p>Using Arrhenius equation we can expand above equation as</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>net</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup><mo>×</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac></math></p><p>Hence,</p><p> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>net</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>3</mn></mrow></msub><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>⇒</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>net</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>60</mn><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>kJ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>mol</mi></math></p>",
    "image": null
  },
